# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file to render the "Cite this repository" button.
cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: "If you use this benchmark, its generator or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "lab-reading-bench: synthetic lab reports with a computed answer key for measuring rule-based and AI readers"
abstract: "A generator of synthetic laboratory reports printed in five national lab styles, conventional and SI units, decimal points and commas, varied flag and range conventions, as text, CSV, FHIR, PDF, page images and phone-style photos, each with an exact answer key; a harness that scores any reader on value accuracy, silent wrong values, critical-value recall and format invariance (the same results printed several ways); and results for a rule-based reader and current LLMs."
version: 0.4.1
date-released: 2026-11-18
# Two licences, by path (LICENSING.md): code (generate.mts, run.mts, images.mts, critical.mts, readers/, corpus/*.mts,
# corpus/*.py, corpus/scripts/, corpus/tests/) is MIT; data and reports (generated reports, pdf/, images/, results/,
# cache/, the built corpus, PREREGISTRATION.md, README.md and other write-ups) are CC BY 4.0. The same split is stated in
# .zenodo.json, whose single licence field carries the data licence (CC BY 4.0) with the code licence in its notes.
